      "id": "a149cfe9-e078-502e-a4b5-9d3df6427335",
      "document_id": "tech/lfi-api-hub/v2.2-rc2/consent-journey/authentication",
      "type": "intro",
      "text": "Authentication\n\nWhen a TPP initiates a consent journey, the API Hub redirects the end user (Payment Services User) to the LFI's Authorization Endpoint so the end user can prove their identity. This is the authentication step — the end user demonstrates to the LFI that they are who they claim to be, using the same credentials and methods they use when accessing the LFI's own digital channels.\n\nAuthentication is distinct from authorization, which is the subsequent step where the authenticated end user reviews and approves the consent (e.g. selecting accounts, confirming a payment).",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "Authentication",
        "source_repo": "Nebras-Open-Finance/community-standards",
